    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1250">

                <pb facs="1240" n="1230" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0093/2–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the
                        Philippines</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-21T18:00:00-05:00">February 21,
                            1949—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>223. Emb instructed close PU camp Mar 1 or sooner if Army withdrawn. Dept will
                    issue orders movement dependents soonest. ReDeptel 241 Feb 18 Emb Nanking
                    requested recommend destination dependents FS personnel. View Embs
                    recommendation Dept perceives no objection <pb facs="1241" n="1231"
                        xml:id="pg1231"/> return Nanking dependents six S[er]v[ic]e Attachés
                    mentioned Nanking’s 431, Feb 21.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d1250-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Manila repeated Nanking, Canton as telCan.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d1250-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1250-f1" n="41" xml:id="d1250-f1-content">
